      {
        "id": "D008",
        "symbol": "AnalyticNotation",
        "type": "notation for calculus, topology and measure",
        "definition": "For maps between the stated normed spaces, Df and fderiv ℝ f denote the real Fréchet derivative (the total library operator, set to zero when no derivative exists); deriv f is the analogous one-variable real derivative. HasDerivAt f a t means f is differentiable at t with derivative a. ContDiffOn and ContDiffAt mean C^r regularity on a set and at a point, with ∞ meaning all finite orders and ω analytic. minSmoothness(κ,2) is 2 for real/complex normed fields and ω otherwise; IsSymmSndFDerivAt κ f p means D(Df)(p)(v)(w)=D(Df)(p)(w)(v) for all directions v,w. 𝓝 t is the neighborhood filter. support f={x:f(x)≠0}, tsupport f is its closure, and HasCompactSupport f means tsupport f is compact. ContinuousOn has its usual relative-set meaning. AEStronglyMeasurable means agreement almost everywhere with a strongly measurable function; Integrable means this measurability and finite integral of the norm, and IntegrableOn f C μ means Integrable f (μ restricted to C). The Bochner integral ∫ f dμ uses the library total convention; it is the ordinary finite Lebesgue integral when f is real and integrable. A set indicator equals its function on the set and zero off it. ae means outside a μ-null set. ‖c‖ₑ denotes the extended nonnegative norm used for ESeminormedAddMonoid; ordinary real numbers have finite extended norm. The standard structure names in source contracts carry their usual mathematical meanings (in particular OpensMeasurableSpace: open sets measurable; BorelSpace: measurable structure is Borel; IsFiniteMeasureOnCompacts: compact sets have finite measure; IsAddHaarMeasure: additive Haar measure).",
        "depends_on": [],
        "requires": [],
        "binders": [],
        "objects": []
      },
