    "inputs": [
      {
        "id": "N001",
        "kind": "internal",
        "statement": "The fixed standard-coordinate representation Space=Fin n→ℝ and Value=Fin m→ℝ identifies the original Euclidean map with ubar restricted to U; Euclidean squares are normSq and the original dx is the product Lebesgue volume dx with no scaling. At positive times V=u_t, A=u_tt, Psp(j)=∂_j u, Ssp(j)=∂_jj u, L=Δ_xu, e=|u_t|²+∑_j|∂_j u|² and E is the same total integral expression, finite whenever e is integrable. The fields ubar,V,A,Psp(j),Ssp(j),W(j),e,d are C∞ on U for every j∈Fin n. For every x∈Space, t>0, k∈Fin m and j∈Fin n: HasDerivAt (r↦ubar(x,r)_k) V(x,t)_k t; HasDerivAt (r↦V(x,r)_k) A(x,t)_k t; HasDerivAt (r↦Psp(j,x,r)_k) W(j,x,t)_k t; fderiv ℝ (y↦ubar(y,t)_k) x (basis(j))=Psp(j,x,t)_k; fderiv ℝ (y↦V(y,t)_k) x (basis(j))=W(j,x,t)_k; and fderiv ℝ (y↦Psp(j,y,t)_k) x (basis(j))=Ssp(j,x,t)_k. In particular the time derivative of Psp(j) and the spatial j derivative of V coincide. Moreover HasDerivAt (r↦e(x,r)) d(x,t) t, with d(x,t)=2 dot(V(x,t),A(x,t))+2∑_j dot(Psp(j,x,t),W(j,x,t)). No assertion of regularity across zero is made.",
