      {
        "id": "N002",
        "kind": "internal",
        "statement": "For every t0>0 there exists a compact C⊆Space such that, writing J=[t0/2,3t0/2] and I=(t0/2,3t0/2), ubar(x,r)=q for all x∉C and r∈J. Every positive-order spacetime derivative of ubar vanishes on Cᶜ×I. In particular V,A,Psp(j),Ssp(j),W(j),e,d vanish there. For every r∈I and j∈Fin n,k∈Fin m, all scalar component spatial sections of V,A,Psp(j),Ssp(j),W(j), the sections e(·,r),d(·,r), and the products V_k A_k, Psp(j)_k W(j)_k, V_k Ssp(j)_k, V_k Psp(j)_k, W(j)_k Psp(j)_k at time r are continuous, have tsupport contained in C, and are dx-integrable. Their finite sums, dot products and finite real linear combinations are likewise continuous, compactly supported in C and integrable. In particular e(·,t) is dx-integrable for every t>0.",
