          "text": "Fix arbitrary t0>0,j∈Fin n,k∈Fin m. On the entire spatial space set f(x)=V(x,t0)_k, g(x)=Psp(j,x,t0)_k and v=basis(j). N001 gives their C∞ regularity as spatial sections: the affine inclusion x↦(x,t0) stays in U and smoothness is local at each point. Thus f and g are differentiable everywhere, in particular on the respective topological supports of g and f. The actual directional derivatives from N001 are Df(x)v=W(j,x,t0)_k and Dg(x)v=Ssp(j,x,t0)_k. By N002 at time t0, all three products (Df v)g, f(Dg v) and fg are continuous with compact support and integrable: they are W(j)_k Psp(j)_k, V_k Ssp(j)_k and V_k Psp(j)_k. Record F001 with these derivative and applicability facts.",
